<p>I didn't realise I use this regularly, but now that I'm on macOS, I'm now aware of this tiny, but useful feature of X11.</p>
<p>You can get X11-like move window by clicking anywhere on it by setting
this flag <code>true</code>:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code><span class="nv">$</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nv">defaults</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nb">write</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">-</span><span class="n">g</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">NSWindowShouldDragOnGesture</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">-</span><span class="n">bool</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">true</span>
</code></pre></div>

<p>and then logout and in again.</p>
<p>It's <code>&lt;cmd&gt;</code> + <code>&lt;ctrl&gt;</code> + <code>&lt;click&gt;</code> rather than <code>&lt;alt&gt;</code> + <code>&lt;click&gt;</code>
but close enough.</p>